   "i": "and so in the end nothing is hard for him.",
   "n": "矣 is not a full stop but a claim about time: the situation has now come about, where it had not before. 'And there it is' is about the tone of it.\n\nOur text carries no closing mark on this unit, because the division into sense-units follows the points where Wang Bi's commentary breaks in, and all the punctuation is a later editor's anyway."
